From: shaohong.dong <shaohong.dong.cq@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] agm: use the codec short name for configuration lookup

Q6A exposes different short and long card names. Use the same name as PAL
instead of deriving calibration paths from the board vendor string. Card
selection still follows the discovered non-USB codec card, not its index.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: shaohong.dong <shaohong.dong.cq@gmail.com>

--- a/service/src/device.c
+++ b/service/src/device.c
@@ -1425,7 +1425,14 @@
         line2[len - 1] = '\0';
 
         if (check_and_update_snd_card(line1)) {
-            card_name = strtok_r(line2, "[:] ", &tmp);
+            /* Use the same short card name as PAL/tinyalsa. The long name
+             * may describe the board vendor/revision instead of the codec.
+             */
+            card_name = strstr(line1, " - ");
+            if (card_name)
+                card_name += 3;
+            else
+                card_name = strtok_r(line2, "[:] ", &tmp);
             if (card_name != NULL) {
                 strlcpy(snd_card_name, card_name, FILE_PATH_EXTN_MAX_SIZE);
                 is_updated = true;
